        "q": "If your GPU runs out of memory while training a CNN, what are five things you could try to solve the problem?",
        "a": "If your GPU runs out of memory while training a CNN, here are five things you could try to solve the problem (other than purchasing a GPU with more RAM):\n- Reduce the mini-batch size.\n- Reduce dimensionality using a larger stride in one or more layers.\n- Remove one or more layers.\n- Use 16-bit floats instead of 32-bit floats.\n- Distribute the CNN across multiple devices."
